      "body": "## Motivation\n\nIn SGLang quantization (`python/sglang/srt/layers/quantization/compressed_tensors/schemes/compressed_tensors_wNa16_moe.py`), `CompressedTensorsWNA16MoE` targets Marlin kernels and therefore enforces:\n\n```python\n    @classmethod\n    def get_min_capability(cls) -> int:\n        # ampere and up\n        return 80\n```\n\nHowever, `CompressedTensorsWNA16TritonMoE` subclasses `CompressedTensorsWNA16MoE` while using pure Triton fused MoE kernels rather than Marlin. Because it did not override `get_min_capability()`, it inherited the `min_capability = 80` requirement.\n\nAs a result, users running W4A16 MoE models (such as `AtomicChat/Unlimited-OCR-2-W4A16`) on Turing (`sm_75`, e.g. Tesla T10, RTX 2080 Ti, Titan RTX) or Volta GPUs were rejected with:\n```\nRuntimeError: Quantization scheme is not supported for the current GPU. Min capability: 80. Current capability: 75\n```\n\nSince Triton MoE kernels natively run on Turing (`sm_75`) and Volta (`sm_70`), this capability check was unnecessarily restrictive.\n\n## Modifications\n\n1. In `CompressedTensorsWNA16TritonMoE`, override `get_min_capability(cls)`:\n```python\n    @classmethod\n    def get_min_capability(cls) -> int:\n        # Triton W4A16 MoE kernels support Turing/Volta (sm_70/sm_75) and up\n        return 70\n```\n2. Allows SGLang to automatically dispatch Triton W4A16 MoE on Turing GPUs without modifying Marlin dense paths.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\n- Tested on Tesla T10 (Turing `sm_75`, 15GB):\n  - Model weights: `AtomicChat/Unlimited-OCR-2-W4A16` (66 experts, uint8 packed).\n  - Cosine Similarity compared to unquantized reference: **1.000000**.\n  - Document parsing outputs identical Markdown structure with zero character corruption.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\n- Tesla T10 (sm_75, 150W):\n  - Decode speed: **63.6 ~ 64.0 token/s**.\n  - Static model memory: **3.13 GB** (reduced from 12 GB FP16).\n  - KV Cache tokens: **120,352 tokens**.\n  - Peak memory: **11.9 GB** with 3.4 GB safety headroom across a 15-page document parsing stress test (17,824 tokens).\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Code formatted according to contribution guidelines.\n- [x] Verified on physical Turing GPU (`sm_75`, Tesla T10).\n- [x] PR title follows `[Feat] [Hardware] scope: title` format.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #41245061969](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41245061969)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41245062022](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41245062022)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #41245061921](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41245061921)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
